{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.PropRigidMonoidalStructuralGapInvariance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.PropRigidMonoidalStructuralGapInvariance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.canonical","kind":"instance","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/prop-rigid-monoidal-structural-gap-invariance.lean#L238-L241","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RigidMonoidalStructuralGapInvarianceAxiom.convention_factorisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RigidMonoidalStructuralGapInvarianceAxiom.convention_factorisation","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/prop-rigid-monoidal-structural-gap-invariance.lean#L233-L233","doc":"The missing input for the convention factorization. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RigidMonoidalStructuralGapInvarianceAxiom.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RigidMonoidalStructuralGapInvarianceAxiom.mk","kind":"ctor","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/prop-rigid-monoidal-structural-gap-invariance.lean#L231-L231","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RigidMonoidalStructuralGapInvarianceAxiom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RigidMonoidalStructuralGapInvarianceAxiom","kind":"class","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/prop-rigid-monoidal-structural-gap-invariance.lean#L208-L233","doc":"**§3b-cond canonical skeleton instance.**  Sets\n`categorical_trace ≡ 0`.  The `sorry` in\n`convention_factorisation` is the **§3b-cond conjectural input**:\nLayer-1 Jones-Wenzl uniqueness of the categorical Markov trace\nτ on `H_n(q)` (Jones 1985, Wenzl 1988).  Per AGENTS.md §3b-cond,\nthis `sorry` is allowed — it encodes the conjectural axiom; all\ndownstream theorems carrying `[R : RigidMonoidalStructuralGapInvariance α]`\nas an explicit hypothesis are unconditional Lean theorems\nmodulo this single conjectural input.\n\nThe data field `categorical_trace _ := 0` is the **weakest**\ncontent-bearing canonical pick (per the trivial-skeleton\nworkplan `docs/audits/2026-05-08-trivial-skeleton-workplan.md`,\npattern A upgrade would pin to a substrate-derived τ value\nonce `MarkovTraceAxiomatic` lands in upstream Mathlib —\nhandover doc §2 P4.A long-term path).\n\nSee the \"Mathlib LP-duality integration sketch\" comment block\nabove for the staged-discharge plan (Layer 1: `MarkovTraceAxiomatic`\ntypeclass; Layer 2: `pair_knot_Z_N_trace_invariance` — done;\nLayer 3: structural induction on the Hecke quadratic).\n\nCompanion: `docs/audits/2026-05-12-lean-p4-canonical-instance-review.md`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.structural_gap_convention_independent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.structural_gap_convention_independent","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/prop-rigid-monoidal-structural-gap-invariance.lean#L144-L159","doc":"**(3) Convention-independence of the structural gap.**  Define\nthe categorical structural gap as `Δ_cat(β) := B_AME -\ncoefficient · |categorical_trace β|`.  Different conventions\nyield the SAME Δ_cat per braid `β` — the convention-dependent\nregularizers cancel because they all factor through the\ncategorical trace.  The body is a one-line rewrite via\n`trace_convention_independence`, which itself follows from\n`R.convention_factorisation`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.convention_equivalence_trans","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.convention_equivalence_trans","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/prop-rigid-monoidal-structural-gap-invariance.lean#L136-L142","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.convention_equivalence_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.convention_equivalence_symm","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/prop-rigid-monoidal-structural-gap-invariance.lean#L129-L134","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.convention_equivalence_refl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.convention_equivalence_refl","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/prop-rigid-monoidal-structural-gap-invariance.lean#L121-L127","doc":"**(2) Convention-equivalence is reflexive and symmetric.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.trace_convention_independence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.trace_convention_independence","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/prop-rigid-monoidal-structural-gap-invariance.lean#L108-L117","doc":"**(1) Convention-independence of the categorical trace.**  Any\ntwo operator-volume conventions agree on the Markov trace of\nany braid `β` — this is the categorical-uniqueness content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RigidMonoidalStructuralGapInvariance.convention_factorisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RigidMonoidalStructuralGapInvariance.convention_factorisation","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/prop-rigid-monoidal-structural-gap-invariance.lean#L96-L96","doc":"Every operator-volume convention factors through it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RigidMonoidalStructuralGapInvariance.categorical_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RigidMonoidalStructuralGapInvariance.categorical_trace","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/prop-rigid-monoidal-structural-gap-invariance.lean#L94-L94","doc":"The unique categorical Markov trace (Jones-Wenzl uniqueness). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RigidMonoidalStructuralGapInvariance.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RigidMonoidalStructuralGapInvariance.mk","kind":"ctor","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/prop-rigid-monoidal-structural-gap-invariance.lean#L92-L92","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RigidMonoidalStructuralGapInvariance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RigidMonoidalStructuralGapInvariance","kind":"class","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/prop-rigid-monoidal-structural-gap-invariance.lean#L76-L98","doc":"**RigidMonoidalStructuralGapInvariance** — the conjectural class.\n\nAn instance asserts that every operator-volume convention `c`\nused in the brane-tower formula factors through the same\ncategorical Markov trace τ.  Concretely:\n\n  `categorical_trace : α → ℝ`            (the unique τ)\n  `convention_factorisation`             (every probed convention\n                                          agrees with the\n                                          categorical trace).\n\nThe non-categorical regularizer is left free per convention,\nencoding the fact that different brane-tower regularizations\ndiffer on the convention-dependent tower part but agree on the\ncategorical τ part. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:rigid-monoidal-structural-gap-invariance","label":"prop:rigid-monoidal-structural-gap-invariance","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/prop-rigid-monoidal-structural-gap-invariance.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.OperatorVolumeConvention.agree_on_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.OperatorVolumeConvention.agree_on_trace","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/prop-rigid-monoidal-structural-gap-invariance.lean#L67-L72","doc":"**Convention-equivalence:** two conventions agree on the\nMarkov trace exactly (categorical) but may differ on the\nregularizer (non-categorical). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.OperatorVolumeConvention.regularizer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.OperatorVolumeConvention.regularizer","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/prop-rigid-monoidal-structural-gap-invariance.lean#L63-L63","doc":"The non-categorical regularizer (brane-tower transient\ncontribution) — convention-DEPENDENT. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.OperatorVolumeConvention.markov_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.OperatorVolumeConvention.markov_trace","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/prop-rigid-monoidal-structural-gap-invariance.lean#L60-L60","doc":"The categorical Markov trace value τ(β_𝔥) — convention-\nINDEPENDENT (unique per Jones-Wenzl). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.OperatorVolumeConvention.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.OperatorVolumeConvention.mk","kind":"ctor","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/prop-rigid-monoidal-structural-gap-invariance.lean#L56-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.OperatorVolumeConvention","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.OperatorVolumeConvention","kind":"structure","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/prop-rigid-monoidal-structural-gap-invariance.lean#L49-L63","doc":"**Abstract operator-volume convention** for evaluating a braid\noperator's contribution to the binding-energy formula.\n\nEach `OperatorVolumeConvention` records a (conjectural)\nconvention-dependent regularizer function and the underlying\nMarkov-trace value it agrees on.  Different conventions vary\n`regularizer`; all share the same `markov_trace`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}